## Delta triple-store SQL Warehouse setting

Context: Delta graph queries and builds shared the global SQL Warehouse with
all other Databricks SQL work. Admins can now pick a dedicated warehouse under
Settings → Triple store → Delta; when unset, the global warehouse is used.

Changes:

1. `src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py`
   Add `delta_warehouse_id` key with get/set helpers.
2. `src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py`
   Add `resolve_delta_warehouse_id`, `get_delta_databricks_credentials`, and
   `get_triplestore_sql_credentials` (Delta backend only).
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaBase.py`, `GraphDBFactory.py`, `health.py`
   Route Delta graph SQL through the Delta warehouse resolver.
4. `src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py`, `src/api/routers/internal/settings.py`
   Expose `delta_warehouse_id` on GET triple-store-backend; add POST
   `/settings/select-delta-warehouse`.
5. `src/front/templates/settings.html`, `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`
   Warehouse dropdown in the Delta section; persisted on global Save.
6. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`, `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py`
   Use Delta-aware credentials for triple-store builds when backend is Delta.
7. `tests/units/settings/test_delta_warehouse_config.py`
   Unit tests for config persistence and warehouse resolution.

